{
  "name": "std-zone-card",
  "description": "Headless zone-guidance mechanic for side-view boards: tracks which band of the world the player is in and holds up that zone's card — name, concept, objective — for a while after every crossing. Listens BODY_MOVED and, when the player's x crosses into a different config zone, stamps the shared entity (zoneId, card, enteredAt) and emits ZONE_CHANGED carrying the card fields; the card self-clears ttlTicks BODY_MOVED ticks later (a per-move tick counter on the entity, so pauses at speed zero still age it out) and boards clear it early via CARD_DISMISS (renamed to a board-scoped progress event) on any mechanic completion. RESTART clears the card and the clock. Renders nothing; boards draw the card from the shared entity (the render authority).",
